/*
    React Vs Angular:
    ==> React:
        1) Library vs. Framework:
        -> React.js is a JavaScript library for building user interfaces, focusing on 
            the view layer.React provides a component-based architecture where 
            components manage their own state and can be composed to build complex UIs.
        2) Virtual DOM:
        3) JSX: React uses JSX (JavaScript XML) for defining component structures 
                within JavaScript code.
        4)  Flexibility: React is more flexible in terms of integrating with other 
            libraries and frameworks. It can be used alongside other technologies 
            without strict conventions.
        5) State Management:
            React encourages the use of libraries like Redux, Context API, or Zustand
            for managing global state across the application.
        6) Learning Curve: 
            React has a relatively shallow learning curve, especially for developers 
            familiar with JavaScript and HTML.
*/

/*
    Angular.js (Angular 1.x):
    1) Framework:
        Angular.js (Angular 1.x) is a full-featured MVC (Model-View-Controller) 
        framework for building web applications. It provides a complete solution with
        built-in features for data binding, dependency injection, routing, and more.
    
    2) Two-Way Data Binding:
        Angular.js features two-way data binding, where changes in the model 
        automatically update the view, and vice versa. This simplifies development but 
        can lead to performance issues with large applications

    3) Direct DOM Manipulation:
        Angular.js manipulates the DOM directly, which can be less efficient compared 
        to React's virtual DOM approach.
    
    4) Template Syntax:
        Angular.js uses declarative templates with custom attributes like ng-model, 
        ng-repeat, etc., to bind data to HTML elements.

    5) Dependency Injection:
        Angular.js provides built-in support for dependency injection, making it 
        easier to manage dependencies and promote modular architecture.
*/

/*
    React Vs Angular
    1) Flexibility vs. Opinionated: 
    React is more flexible and lightweight, suitable for component-centric development. 
    Angular.js (Angular 1.x) is more opinionated and provides a full-featured 
    framework with built-in solutions for many aspects of application development.

    2) Performance: React's virtual DOM can offer better performance optimizations 
       compared to Angular.js's direct DOM manipulation, especially in complex 
       applications with frequent updates.

    3) Learning Curve: React tends to have a gentler learning curve, while Angular.js 
        (Angular 1.x) may require more upfront investment due to its comprehensive 
        feature set and conventions.

*/